                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>
                        Evidence<font class="required1">*</font>
                    </td>
                    <td>
                        @Html.DropDownListFor(x => x.Answer4Evidence, new List<SelectListItem>() { new SelectListItem() { Text = "Yes", Value = "Yes" }, new SelectListItem() { Text = "No", Value = "No" } }, "Please Select", new { id = "Answer4Evidence", @class = "form-control", required = "required", onchange = "CheckValueAndMakeFieldMandatory('Yes', 'Answer4Evidence', 'Answer4Filename', true)" })
                        @Html.ValidationMessageFor(x => x.Answer4Evidence, null, new { @class = "validation-error" })
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr id="trAnswer4Filename" style="display:none">
                    <td colspan="2">
                        Upload Evidence<font class="required1">*</font>
                        <br />
                        <div class="upload-container" id="dropArea4">

                            <i class="fa fa-cloud-upload upload-icon"></i>

                            <h3>Drag & Drop Files Here</h3>
                            <p>or click below to browse files</p>

                            <input type="file"
                                   name="Answer4Filename"
                                   onchange="ValidatingFileUpload('Answer4Filename')"
                                   id="Answer4Filename"
                                   class="form-control file-input" />


                        </div>

                        @Html.ValidationMessageFor(x => x.Answer4Filename, null, new { @class = "validation-error" })
                    </td>

                </tr>






                <tr>
                    <td>
                        5. Have you spent any time dealing with the consequences of the LAA
                        data breach? For example, changing passwords,monitoring bank
                        accounts and credit reports, or contacting your bank to report fraud or
                        cancel cards. If yes, please confirm what, how much time was spent
                        and why<font class="required1">*</font>
                    </td>
                    <td>
                        @Html.TextAreaFor(x => x.Answer5, new { @class = "form-control", autocomplete = "off", rows = "5", required = "required" })

                        @Html.ValidationMessageFor(x => x.Answer5, null, new { @class = "validation-error" })
                        <br />
                        <div style="width:100%; background-color:lightgray">

                        </div>
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td colspan="2" style="width:100%; background-color:lightgray">
                        <p>
                            In order to secure compensation, you must be able to provide evidence of distress and not just say you were
                            upset by the breach<br /><br />
                            <b>Best evidence:</b> GP notes, prescriptions, counselling records and sick notes.
                            <b>Good evidence:</b>Diary entries made at the time, emails/ messages to friends and witness statements.
                            <b>Weak evidence:</b> No supporting proof.
                            <br /><br />
                            <b>Be specific:</b> What symptoms(e.g.sleep problems, appetite changes, anxiety/ panic attacks, low mood,
                            difficulty concentrating, hypervigilance, physical symptoms such as headaches / stomach tension, increased
                            alcohol / substances)? When did the symptoms start? How severe were they? How long did they last? What
                            did they make you stop doing? Who noticed these? Are they still ongoing?
                        </p>
                    </td>
                </tr>




                <tr>
                    <td>
